# Terraform
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
backend.hcl

# terraform/bootstrap/backend.tf is NOT like environments/*/backend.tf: it's
# a *complete* S3 backend block with the account's real bucket name hardcoded
# inline (bootstrap can't use a partial backend.tf + backend-config the way
# environments do, since bootstrapping is what creates that bucket in the
# first place). Committing it breaks terraform/README.md's documented
# fresh-account flow: "terraform init" in bootstrap/ auto-loads any backend
# block already on disk, so a fresh clone would try to init against BU's
# existing bucket instead of starting on local state. Keep it local-only,
# created from backend.tf.example per the README's step 2, same as every
# environment's gitignored backend.hcl.
terraform/bootstrap/backend.tf

